-- title:
--   Residues of Gauss-integral level-M' functions give F_κ(Γ₀(M'))
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and $M'\ge 1$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with residue field $\kappa=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$. Let $R$ be a regular prolongation of $A$ from $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to $F=$ `fieldBar q M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the field `xHFunctionField (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with residue target the $\kappa$-subfield $\mathrm{qExpFunctionFieldC}$ of $\kappa((q))$ generated by quotients of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms for `GammaH (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`; thus $R$ provides a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F$ with a surjective residue map whose kernel is the maximal ideal, extending the residue map of $A$. Assume $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A$; that $f\in R.\mathrm{integers}$ holds exactly when $f\cdot y=x$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ for Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero coefficientwise reduction; and that every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image lies in $F$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with residue the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Then the residue map carries those $f\in R.\mathrm{integers}$ whose $q$-expansion lies in `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma0 M'))` into $\mathrm{qExpFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,(\Gamma_0(M'))\subseteq\kappa((q))$, and every element of the latter is the residue of such an $f$.
--
--   This is the Deuring-style reduction statement in $q$-expansion form, asserting compatibility of the Gauss prolongation at level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ with the level-$\Gamma_0(M')$ subfield: the residue map sends the intersection of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with the base-changed level-$M'$ function field onto the level-$M'$ function field over the residue field. It feeds the identification of the Galois action on the reduced curve used in the `comap_levelAutBar_eq_of_redQ_smul_lineInfty_eq` family of results.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_residue_mem_qExpFunctionFieldC_gamma0_and_surj.lean

